    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 213</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_213/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 11 Apr 2025 19:46:59 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_213/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;What is the output of the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;package main&#xA;&#xA;import (  &#xA;    &amp;#34;fmt&amp;#34;&#xA;)&#xA;&#xA;func main() {  &#xA;    a := [5]int{1, 2, 3, 4, 5}&#xA;    t := a[3:4:4]&#xA;    fmt.Println(t[0])&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;A.3&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;B.4&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;C.compilation error&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;B&#xA;&lt;a href=&#34;https://go.dev/play/p/z3KqBXFXMm3&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;external nofollow noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;Run online&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Answer:&lt;/strong&gt; B&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key takeaway:&lt;/strong&gt; Go Language Slice Operator &lt;code&gt;[i:j:k]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analysis:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Array Initialization:&lt;/strong&gt;&#xA;&lt;code&gt;a := [5]int{1, 2, 3, 4, 5}&lt;/code&gt; creates an array &lt;code&gt;a&lt;/code&gt; containing 5 integers. Its content is &lt;code&gt;[1, 2, 3, 4, 5]&lt;/code&gt;, with indices from 0 to 4.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 156</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_156/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 09 Jan 2025 20:27:59 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_156/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;What are the length and capacity of slices a, b, and c respectively?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;package main&#xA;&#xA;import (&#xA;    &amp;#34;fmt&amp;#34;&#xA;)&#xA;&#xA;func main() {&#xA;    s := [3]int{1, 2, 3}&#xA;    a := s[:0]&#xA;    b := s[:2]&#xA;    c := s[1:2:cap(s)]&#xA;&#xA;    fmt.Println(len(a), cap(a))&#xA;    fmt.Println(len(b), cap(b))&#xA;    fmt.Println(len(c), cap(c))&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;a: Length and capacity 0 3&#xA;b: Length and capacity 2 3&#xA;c: Length and capacity 1 2&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://go.dev/play/p/QHiuY9qh4pw&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;external nofollow noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;Run online&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 class=&#34;heading-element&#34; id=&#34;key-takeaway-array-or-slice-slicing-operations&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Key Takeaway: Array or Slice Slicing Operations&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;a href=&#34;#key-takeaway-array-or-slice-slicing-operations&#34; class=&#34;heading-mark&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;svg class=&#34;octicon octicon-link&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 16 16&#34; version=&#34;1.1&#34; width=&#34;16&#34; height=&#34;16&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Slicing operations can have 2 or 3 parameters, such as &lt;code&gt;[i:j]&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;[i:j:k]&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 137</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_137/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 21 Dec 2024 01:24:56 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_137/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;What is the output of the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;package main&#xA;&#xA;import (  &#xA;    &amp;#34;fmt&amp;#34;&#xA;)&#xA;&#xA;func main() {  &#xA;    a := [5]int{1, 2, 3, 4, 5}&#xA;    t := a[3:4:4]&#xA;    fmt.Println(t[0])&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;A.3&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;B.4&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;C.compilation error&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;B &lt;a href=&#34;https://go.dev/play/p/z3KqBXFXMm3&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;external nofollow noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;Run online&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;a&lt;/code&gt; is an array of length 5 with elements 1, 2, 3, 4, 5.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;t := baseStr[low:high:max]&lt;/code&gt;&#xA;&lt;code&gt;low&lt;/code&gt; specifies the starting element index, &lt;code&gt;high&lt;/code&gt; specifies the ending element index (exclusive), and &lt;code&gt;max&lt;/code&gt; specifies the maximum index the slice can grow to.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
